Completed [RESULT.md](<./RESULT.md>), [PROOF.md](<./PROOF.md>) and the progress/handoff files. The general bound remains open.

Two concrete obstructions are proved:

- The tower inclusion is reversed. The window \(2\pi ux/L\) reaches dimension \(ux/v_a\), so it favors slow sectors.
- An unfiltered ring trace cannot have the proposed uniform bound. Two XX chains at fixed \(d=4\), \(M=1\), \(N(1)=1\) give an arbitrarily large infrared excitation trace as one chain becomes slow, while \(A=2M\).

A precise sufficient lemma is recorded. If the central charge \(C_j\) in
\[
4eM\,2^{-j-1}<v_a\le4eM\,2^{-j}
\]
satisfies \(C_j\le K(d)2^{j/2}\), then
\[
A\le4e(2+\sqrt2)\,M K(d).
\]
The missing step is a lattice bound on velocity-resolved infrared state content. Lieb–Robinson and information capacity alone did not supply it.

Free-fermion, XX-stack and qualified slow-construction checks are included. All small numerical checks passed. No heavy numerics or files outside `work_C115` were used or modified.

